\date{2025-11-29T18:59:16Z}
\title{Defining functions in Disco}

\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{We can define our own functions in [[0027]].  First, we give the name of
the function and its [type](002B), which will be something like
\tt{A -> B} where \tt{A} is the type of the function's inputs,
and \tt{B} is the type of the outputs.  Then we define what output
the function should give for each input.
\pre\verb<<<|
double : N -> N
double(n) = 2n<<<
If we write the above definition of \tt{double} in a
\tt{.disco} file, we can load it at the Disco prompt using the
\tt{:load} command, then try it on some inputs:
\pre\verb<<<|
Disco> :load double.disco
Loading double.disco...
Loaded.
Disco> double(2)
4
Disco> double(7)
14<<<
}